---
/**
 * Cloudflare Turnstile challenge for the enquiry forms.
 *
 * Why this exists: the pages are built to rank on commercial terms, and a
 * ranking form gets scraped. The forms already carry a honeypot and submit
 * through fetch rather than a native POST, which turns away the naive half of
 * that traffic. What neither stops is the deliberate case, because the
 * Web3Forms access key sits in the page source: anyone can read it and POST
 * straight to the API, skipping the honeypot, the JavaScript and this widget
 * together.
 *
 * So the widget is only half the fix. The other half is switching captcha
 * verification ON in the Web3Forms dashboard, which makes the API reject any
 * submission without a valid token no matter where it came from. Turnstile is
 * the free, no-interaction option and needs no cookie banner.
 *
 * Renders nothing at all until a sitekey is set, so it ships inert and the
 * forms behave exactly as they do now.
 *
 * The token rides along automatically: Turnstile writes a hidden
 * `cf-turnstile-response` input into the surrounding form, and every form here
 * serialises with `Object.fromEntries(new FormData(form))`.
 */
import { turnstileKey } from "../lib/site";
---
{turnstileKey && (
  <>
    <div class="cf-turnstile" data-sitekey={turnstileKey} data-appearance="interaction-only" data-size="flexible" style="margin-top:14px"></div>
    <script is:inline>
      // One page can hold more than one form; load the API once.
      if (!document.getElementById("cf-turnstile-api")) {
        const s = document.createElement("script");
        s.id = "cf-turnstile-api";
        s.src = "https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js";
        s.async = true;
        s.defer = true;
        document.head.appendChild(s);
      }
    </script>
  </>
)}
